{"connection_id": "BC-238ddcaf4901c5fbffa7", "ref": "Wisdom of Solomon 7:2", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "flesh molded in the womb", "note": "Solomon describes being molded in flesh in his mother's womb over ten months, a direct gestational counterpart to the commentary's fetal formation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-ee41d6cc5c4e35fb9f7c", "ref": "Wisdom of Solomon 7:2", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "paralel", "basis": "ten months, blood, and seed", "note": "The next verse describes gestation in a fixed period and bodily material from seed and blood. Its timed, material account closely meets the commentary's womb gathering and measured formation."}
