{"connection_id": "BC-8eecb8ed0d601cdc1e8a", "ref": "Wisdom of Solomon 7:4", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "swaddling and infant care", "note": "Solomon says he was swaddled and cared for, giving a concrete childhood instance of the commentary's branch of Rabb as raising a child."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cbb952cb9017238ccd5e", "ref": "Wisdom of Solomon 7:5", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "king begins life like everyone", "note": "Even a king's birth has no different beginning; this Jewish reflection makes the commentary's bodily life stages universal rather than a lexical claim about one person."}
